Fascinating.  I've never tried canceling stuff in a shop door
before.  But I've had a bunch of shop experiences, though,
I've some replies to some of the posts in this thread:

Seems to me, the square two-squares-inside the shop,
one-square-inside, in-the-door, and outside-the-door
have four very different properties!

Two squares inside, and you're solidly "in" a shop.  Anything
you pick up that you didn't drop and immediately pick back
up again without selling, if you pick it up, you're charged.

One-square-inside is both sort-of-inside and sort-of-outside
the shop.  The shop keeper won't warn you about unpaid items
there.  (Probably for convenience so you can pass back and
forth over that spot without repeated warnings.)  If your pet
drops a stolen item there (or if you find some item there and
pick it up) you won't be charged.  But oddly, if you shoplift
it YOURSELF and drop it there, then leave, the shopkeeper will
call the kops.  Also, if you drop anything of your own on this
square and walk even one step away, the shopkeeper may jump
on it and claim it as his own.  (I died that way a while back,
trying to get my stuff back from a shopkeeper who had
"finders-keepers"'ed it.)

In-the-door is the "warn zone".  The shopkeeper will warn you
if you enter this square with unpaid stuff.  ("Elendil, please
don't leave without paying!")  But he shouldn't care if you
do stuff to things you already paid for.  Same for the
inside of the shop.  If he does, it's a bug, I'd say.
It should go:
"You zap your potions with your wand of cancellation.
Mr. Olsen looks disinterested."
I'll have to try that and see what happens to me.
(Hmmm...  That bug doesn't exist with armor.  I bought some
cursed armor, took it outside, took it back to the doorway,
cancelled it.  Shopkeeper didn't mind.  Couldn't find a
liquor shop or I'd try it with potions.)

Outside-the-door is obviously solidly-outside the shop.  You
go here without paying, the shopkeeper will call the kops,
and sometimes chase after you with a /oS and kill you.  And
yes, you can get here easily.  I did that a few days ago
by wearing rings of teleport and teleport-control.  First I
murdered a bunch of kops, then the shopkeeper came after me
and said "Elendil, you're a thief!"  I said, "Is that so?"
and chopped him to mincemeat with Stormbringer.  :-)


